# Repo-wide ignores only. Each service (web/, api/) has its own
# .gitignore for its build output and dependencies — a single root-level
# pattern like "/node_modules" only anchors to the repo root and would
# silently fail to ignore web/node_modules or api/node_modules, which is
# exactly the kind of thing that looks fine locally and then shows up as
# a multi-hundred-megabyte accidental commit. See web/.gitignore and
# api/.gitignore.

.DS_Store
*.pem
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.vercel

# Safety net only — nothing should ever run `npm install` from the repo
# root (there's no root package.json). If this ever matches something,
# that's a sign a command ran in the wrong directory, not a normal case.
/node_modules
/.next/
